      "writtenOn": "2019-03-29T08:09:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack!\n\nwhen calling the \u0027iret\u0027, cpu will auto save current cpu\u0027s context including the next execute instruction (here is the begging of the while loop ) into aon_tss (eip field for next execute instruction). so next time, when main FW switch to aontask, will start execute from the code which pointed by the eip field in aon_tss. \n\nwe initialized the aon_tss\u0027s eip value with the ish_aon_main() address, so the first time, the aontask start run from ish_aon_main(). but from \nthe second time, will always start execute from the begging of the while loop.",
      "parentUuid": "372b6cf3_13229f24",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 340,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 340,
        "endChar": 57
      },
